[{:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33986"] :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=4+3t \\\\ y=3+4t \\\\ z=-2+6t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x+5y+8z=229.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x+5y+8z & =229 \\\\ 2(4+3t)+5(3+4t)+8(-2+6t) & =229 \\\\ 8+6t+15+20t-16+48t & =229 \\\\ 74t & =222 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+3(3)=13 \\\\ y=3+4(3)=15 \\\\ z=-2+6(3)=16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(13,15,16).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-33987/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "46499e9f-2421-5073-8b5f-8a92d43805eb" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33987/selection/6f8cd113d0e8213e5ea82e53a3bf78aa5c2324f9fec4f62aa9493a3e056307cb" :answer/id #uuid "442f8d07-d442-5966-af16-0a1adb12fbc4" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(9,5,3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33987/selection/8ce8310f7013f52b8f1896b67a5384914d2d800560e86ac5c3e6d0c256cb2778" :answer/id #uuid "c9e93674-08ab-5156-a97c-e6b26e2d1934" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(3,5,9)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33987/selection/99a0ce0bb9fd964725c095f5442f9a8b7c4cc6d037e824104f520286d476d52c" :answer/id #uuid "49066f88-8216-564b-a1d2-7cdc03998fea" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,-1,6)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33987/selection/6cbedd9f530dd8c11492a1b608e84924fa88f60330535e1eb1c0a0952ade71a2" :answer/id #uuid "e9a8717a-e212-55ad-8b4a-a5d2b7477ad8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,4,2)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-33987/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "2fb6d432-3990-5462-9174-0583dac17339" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-33987/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer-field/choices ["q-33987/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" "q-33987/selection/6f8cd113d0e8213e5ea82e53a3bf78aa5c2324f9fec4f62aa9493a3e056307cb" "q-33987/selection/8ce8310f7013f52b8f1896b67a5384914d2d800560e86ac5c3e6d0c256cb2778" "q-33987/selection/99a0ce0bb9fd964725c095f5442f9a8b7c4cc6d037e824104f520286d476d52c" "q-33987/selection/6cbedd9f530dd8c11492a1b608e84924fa88f60330535e1eb1c0a0952ade71a2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-33987" :question/id #uuid "cbfd2820-3a30-53a2-832d-407032fe3cf1" :question/math-academy-id "q-33987" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:r=⟨3,5,9⟩+t⟨4,-1,6⟩,\\,Π:-2x+4y+2z-16=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "Let's start by writing the equation of the line as\n\n$$\nr=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩.\n$$\n\nLet's also write the equation of the plane in the dot product form:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}-2x+4y+2z-16 & =0 \\\\ -2x+4y+2z & =16 \\\\ ⟨x,y,z⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ ⟨3+4t,5-t,9+6t⟩\\cdot ⟨-2,4,2⟩ & =16 \\\\ -2(3+4t)+4(5-t)+2(9+6t) & =16 \\\\ -6-8t+20-4t+18+12t & =16 \\\\ 32 & =16.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe equation has no solution. Therefore, we conclude that the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ do not intersect." :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-33987/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-33987"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id [:question/math-academy-id "q-33992"] :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2t \\\\ y=-1+4t \\\\ z=-3-5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:2x-5y+3z-84=0.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-5y+3z-84 & =0 \\\\ 2(5-2t)-5(-1+4t)+3(-3-5t) & =84 \\\\ 10-4t+5-20t-9-15t & =84 \\\\ -39t & =78 \\\\ t & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=-2$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=5-2(-2)=9 \\\\ y=-1+4(-2)=-9 \\\\ z=-3-5(-2)=7\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is  $P(9,-9,7).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id "q-108368/selection/e28a61df108e33525d8b3e530bd9d6659fa64fb66c5ec7cd5fd759e73f6d44dd" :answer/id #uuid "7e39da6c-a7b5-5af6-b99d-edf48043b61e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(10,9,15)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108368/selection/41955e99c6adce5756d5b8a8367a06b88c01011ee4110a364bbfe17cc6c17079" :answer/id #uuid "42068190-cf84-57fe-bbaf-140c2463d46e" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(20,29,40)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108368/selection/6f0baa004b20bdbccc655e8ace3705aebbd0aa17a9fa371a0b8bf646808996bf" :answer/id #uuid "527a7770-d5f8-5a3d-8f3c-9ed5af2d3a60" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-6,-23,-25)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108368/selection/a027e324dc850d746a27b1d37d1a09ff920b89f101d8cedbc9d45d73454cf487" :answer/id #uuid "f5d807c9-264d-511a-9190-73c4168381a9" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(2,-7,-5)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108368/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "66f3bab9-e5a6-5f04-94ae-e823f168663e" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108368/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "85b5821d-cbb8-5c03-9816-ea997524331b" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108368/selection/e28a61df108e33525d8b3e530bd9d6659fa64fb66c5ec7cd5fd759e73f6d44dd" :answer-field/choices ["q-108368/selection/e28a61df108e33525d8b3e530bd9d6659fa64fb66c5ec7cd5fd759e73f6d44dd" "q-108368/selection/41955e99c6adce5756d5b8a8367a06b88c01011ee4110a364bbfe17cc6c17079" "q-108368/selection/6f0baa004b20bdbccc655e8ace3705aebbd0aa17a9fa371a0b8bf646808996bf" "q-108368/selection/a027e324dc850d746a27b1d37d1a09ff920b89f101d8cedbc9d45d73454cf487" "q-108368/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108368" :question/id #uuid "3ee9813a-b1b3-5ef0-86f7-ac30b2000775" :question/math-academy-id "q-108368" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2t \\\\ y=-3+4t \\\\ z=5t\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,Π:3x+2y-z=33.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We can substitute the parametric expressions for $x,$ $y,$ and $z$ of the line into the equation of the plane immediately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3x+2y-z & =33 \\\\ 3(4+2t)+2(-3+4t)-(5t) & =33 \\\\ 12+6t-6+8t-5t & =33 \\\\ 9t & =27 \\\\ t & =3\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTo get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P$, we substitute $t=3$ into the parametric equations of the line:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}x=4+2(3)=10 \\\\ y=-3+4(3)=9 \\\\ z=5(3)=15\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the intersection point is $P(10,9,15).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-108368/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "82e761b5-ec1c-549d-b726-e0909cfe460b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108368"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-108891/selection/4603caf1a6414a8f78c976caa08677a08ec22309062239dd2706f02fd64a1011" :answer/id #uuid "79a653c8-b4aa-594e-99f5-7bdd4b9ec4c0" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(-2,0,1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108891/selection/4f2a1b151cee4fef5f394221d7217d3cbc2371a74ad5384c30183f069bbcbea0" :answer/id #uuid "b37cdbe3-b6af-5b8b-8187-a7041d20b8b8" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(1,4,-1)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108891/selection/9499bbfac97e5e4f7a47ad5086590c8a8338873844d4d80b9e965ca569751568" :answer/id #uuid "6d2a8077-a027-5fd7-8c52-7fa90052e334" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(5,4,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108891/selection/aa69c48a96d3ef82eecb97b8c691c30fa7a4631acebac36cbc572e7b39851f63" :answer/id #uuid "a9d396de-d5f4-5ba4-a270-d0a28f1f0cae" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "(4,8,-3)" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108891/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368" :answer/id #uuid "800ecb37-1966-513c-b261-63d50c33f347" :answer/type :answer.type/text :answer/value "No intersection" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-108891/selection" :answer-field/id #uuid "a62b7884-84dc-538a-9bba-dca997f72e34" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/radio :answer-field/correct "q-108891/selection/4f2a1b151cee4fef5f394221d7217d3cbc2371a74ad5384c30183f069bbcbea0" :answer-field/choices ["q-108891/selection/4603caf1a6414a8f78c976caa08677a08ec22309062239dd2706f02fd64a1011" "q-108891/selection/4f2a1b151cee4fef5f394221d7217d3cbc2371a74ad5384c30183f069bbcbea0" "q-108891/selection/9499bbfac97e5e4f7a47ad5086590c8a8338873844d4d80b9e965ca569751568" "q-108891/selection/aa69c48a96d3ef82eecb97b8c691c30fa7a4631acebac36cbc572e7b39851f63" "q-108891/selection/c8041c0b45c7624d574ce5092ae47ec9f4b5f3ba950a413ae68bb2ab9ecc7368"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-108891" :question/id #uuid "51708de4-81da-5999-acf1-9c92facc1391" :question/math-academy-id "q-108891" :question/problem "Find the intersection point of the line $l$ and the plane $Π$ with equations\n\n$$\nl:\\frac{x+2}{3}=\\frac{y}{4}=\\frac{1-z}{2},\\,Π:r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩=-9.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "From the equation of the line $l$, we know that it passes through the point $A(-2,0,1)$ and it is parallel to the vector $v=⟨3,4,-2⟩.$ Therefore, its vector equation is given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r & =⟨-2,0,1⟩+t⟨3,4,-2⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ).$\n\nNow, substituting $r=⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩$ into the equation of the plane, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}r\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ ⟨-2+3t,4t,1-2t⟩\\cdot ⟨4,-3,1⟩ & =-9 \\\\ 4(-2+3t)-3(4t)+(1-2t) & =-9 \\\\ -8+12t-12t+1-2t & =-9 \\\\ -2t & =-2 \\\\ t & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, to get the position vector $p$ of the intersection point $P,$ we substitute $t=1$ into the equation of the line:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}p & =⟨-2+3(1),4(1),1-2(1)⟩ \\\\  & =⟨1,4,-1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, we get $P(1,4,-1).$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-108891/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "caf29808-4551-56a0-ac86-a4587a06fc0f"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-108891"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
